<rect x="115" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<rect x="152" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<line x1="6" y1="44" x2="184" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="6" y1="39" x2="6" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="184" y1="39" x2="184" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<text x="95" y="62" font-size="13" fill="#2A2F5E" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">5 white</text>
<rect x="189" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<rect x="226" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<rect x="263" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<rect x="300" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<rect x="337" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<rect x="374" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#466BAA"/>
<line x1="191" y1="44" x2="406" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="191" y1="39" x2="191" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="406" y1="39" x2="406" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<text x="298.5" y="62" font-size="13" fill="#2A2F5E" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">6 blue</text>
<rect x="411" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<rect x="448" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<rect x="485" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<rect x="522" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<rect x="559" y="4" width="34" height="30" rx="4" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#2A2F5E" stroke-width="1"/>
<line x1="413" y1="44" x2="591" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="413" y1="39" x2="413" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="591" y1="39" x2="591" y2="44" stroke="#466BAA" stroke-width="2"/>
<text x="502" y="62" font-size="13" fill="#2A2F5E" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">5 white</text>
</svg>
Text works the same way: AAAAAABBBCCCCC becomes 6A 3B 5C. RLE suits icons and cartoons with large areas of one colour, but not photos: ABCD would become 1A 1B 1C 1D — bigger than before!
@end

@row
@box alt | Lossless 2 · Dictionary methods
A repeated sequence is stored once; each later copy becomes a short reference to it. Ideal when a word such as *computer* appears again and again. Used in ZIP, PNG and GIF.
@end
@box alt | Lossless 3 · Huffman coding
Common characters get **short** binary codes and rare ones longer codes, instead of 8 bits each: in English, *e* might get 3 bits and *z* 10. ZIP and PNG use it with a dictionary method.
@end
@endrow

@box dark | Lossy techniques
- **JPEG images:** works on 8 × 8 pixel blocks, reducing fine detail and colour information the eye hardly notices (our eyes are more sensitive to brightness than to colour).
- **MP3 and AAC sound:** removes sounds people cannot hear, and quiet sounds *masked* by louder ones; a song shrinks to about a tenth of its CD size.
- **Video (MP4):** most of a scene stays the same, so only the **changes** between frames are stored, and each frame is compressed like a JPEG.
- **Lower settings:** a lower resolution, colour depth or sampling rate also shrinks files.
@end

@try
Use RLE to compress AAAABBBBBBCCDDDDD and count how many values you save. Then explain why RLE works badly on a photograph.
@end



@page Process execution
@section 1.3 Computer Architecture & The Von Neumann Model
@plane none

A program is a list of instructions; **process execution** is how the CPU carries them out. Almost every computer follows a design described by John von Neumann in 1945: the **Von Neumann architecture**.

Its key idea is the **stored-program concept**: instructions and data are stored **together in the same main memory**, and the CPU fetches the instructions one at a time. Early computers such as ENIAC had to be rewired for each new job; a stored-program computer just loads a different program.

